      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 The Authors. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "The regulation of site-specific pigmentation in reconstructs used for skin grafting is incompletely understood. Using an engineered skin equivalent model, Klar et al. incorporated adipose-derived mesenchymal cells into skin substitutes and found that adipose-derived mesenchymal cells secreted high levels of transforming growth factor-β1, which down-regulates melanogenic enzymes such as tyrosinase to decrease melanin synthesis and prevent normal pigmentation of resulting skin grafts."
      },
